                    briefing_text_r2:       `Allocate the short supply under a service-level objective. Choose your <strong>service level</strong> — equity-weighted to close the hill gap, or throughput to maximise raw doses — then split the safety-stock <strong>buffer between central and edge</strong>. Central buffer is elegant on paper, but the hill blocks are an 11-hour round trip and cannot be resupplied mid-week: the buffer that protects your wards is the buffer your remote sites will <em>never see in time</em>. And size your vials for the session — 10-dose vials in 4-child hill sessions burn supply you do not have.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Choose the distribution route`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Design the routing for the cold-chain fleet inside the 3,400 vial-equivalent capacity and the <strong>4-hour cold-chain breach limit</strong>. Hub-and-spoke milk-runs are cheapest on transport — but reach the last hill site past hour 5 and the doses arrive non-viable, so you save ₹1.8 lakh in transport and destroy ₹6 lakh of vaccine. Dedicated remote runs (₹0.62 lakh per cycle) and a motorcycle cold-box leg protect equity and the cold chain. Decide route, cycle count, and how hard to protect the temperature clock — and watch <em>cost per dose delivered</em>, not cost per dose shipped.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Write the triage rule & recover`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Supply is still short of demand. Publish an explicit <strong>triage rule</strong> for who gets the last dose when a site runs low — by coverage-deficit and outbreak risk, by age, or first-come-first-served. Refusing to write one is itself a rule: it defaults to FCFS, which protects the mobile urban families and fails exactly the children you are behind on. Then a day-22 shock hits — a hill-block cluster plus a further 5% supply slip — and the funder offers nothing extra. Hold your rule or scramble? Stay inside <strong>₹3.8 crore</strong>, or borrow coverage from next quarter's infants?`,

