                    insight_equitable:      `Equitable coverage: you cleared ≥90% AND closed the hill–urban gap to within 8 points, inside the ₹3.8 crore envelope. The same scarce dose, designed well across inventory, routing and triage, protected the children the campaign was behind on.`,
                    insight_overran:        `You hit the coverage number but blew the ₹3.8 crore envelope — and that overrun comes straight out of next quarter's routine immunisation. You did not remove the harm, you shifted it onto next quarter's infants.`,
                    insight_throughput:     `Throughput win, equity lost: coverage looks good but the hill–urban gap is still wide. You optimised for doses shipped, not children protected — and the highest-outbreak-risk blocks are the ones you left behind.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the ≥90% funder target. Week-3 coverage below the line risks the 'campaign at risk' review and doses reallocated to a neighbouring operator. Re-examine where you left effective supply, equity or the cold chain on the table.`,
                    insight_coldchain:      `A cold-chain breach destroyed doses on arrival at least once — those doses were non-viable, so your true cost per dose delivered is higher than the transport bill suggested. Cold chain is a hard constraint.`,
                    insight_abandoned:      `Under pressure you abandoned equity for the urban wards — the headline number survived, but the hill blocks with the highest outbreak risk fell further behind. That is the implicit triage rule the campaign exists to override.`,
                    insight_wastage:        `Open-vial wastage shrank your effective supply below the nominal allocation — the counter-intuitive driver of the coverage gap. Vial sizing and session batching, not volume, were the lever that moved it.`,
